+    // [ff9mapkit netsync s161] THE ATE RELAY (studies/field-coop/ATE-RELAY.md; GUEST-TRAVERSAL-TWO-PC.md "For later patches"). THE DEFECT
+    // (the 2026-10-28 two-PC session, 352 "Vivi, Confused"): each copy draws the ATE icon itself, but the menu opens only on a Select read
+    // with control ON -- `if (usercontrol == 1 && byte238 == 1 && B_KEYON(Select)) { ... WindowSync(1, 64, 98) ... }` in Code1's loop --
+    // and the host relays only control-OFF reads (NetSyncClient.TapScriptKeyIfHost) while the guest masks its own Select on control-on
+    // reads (MISC-08). So the guest's copy never opened the menu, the title card or the white fade, and the follow carried it to 350.
+    // THE CENSUS (two counts, ATE-RELAY.md): every control-on Select read in the shipping game (150 fields, one each) is an ATE menu gate,
+    // and every one of those menus ORs Cancel in as row 15 (`EnableDialogChoices(mask | 32768, 0)`).
+    //
+    // HOST   TapScriptKeyIfHost's control-on branch notes a Select hit (ArmHostPress). The raw read is never relayed (`&&` does not
+    //        short-circuit in the VM: the read runs every frame, and a press with the ATE unavailable opens nothing). ETb.NewMesWin's hook
+    //        (OnWindowOpened) relays it when an ATE-caption window opens, run by THAT reader on THAT field within ArmTicks key ticks
+    //        (HostRelays): ring kind 3 (NetSyncDialog.KindAte) [uid][text][win][the menu's cancel row]. The title card opens seconds later,
+    //        a compulsory grey ATE has no Select hit: neither relays.
+    // GUEST  the ring merge hands kind 3 here (Ingest) as the PENDING PRESS (the newest; an older press's stale choice events are dropped
+    //        when this copy's menu opens: NetSyncDialog.DropStaleChoices). FilterScriptButtons' control-on branch ORs Select into that
+    //        reader's reads on that field (ServeRule) -- every key tick, never consumed, because a served key is spent whether or not the
+    //        guest's gate is true -- until the guest's own ATE MENU (a choice window with the ATE caption) opens, run by that reader
+    //        (OpenRetires: the retire, and the proof). Its life: kept while its field is mine, my follow-warp's or the host's (or the host's
+    //        field is unknown: a blip, a load) -- PressKeep -- and the inbox keeps the host's later events for that field while it waits
+    //        (PressHoldsEvent), so the press and its answer live and die together; kept across a landing on its own field; dropped once
+    //        the host has left its field and come back (PressRoundTripOver: the host's ATE is over); expired after PressTtlMs counted only
+    //        while I stand there with my control on, and at PressCapMs from its arrival; dropped when the dialogue session resets.
+    // THE EPISODE (from that open): HUB phase on the menu's field. The lock closing the menu on the host's EXACT row is the host's pick
+    //        (ByHostRule; a host row masked on a census-shaped menu closes it with Cancel instead: UsesCancelFallback). The pick lapses the
+    //        first tick my control is back (a Cancel / Leave branch hands control back; a branch that jumps never does before its Field()).
+    //        While it stands, the copy's own Field(dest) passes RedirectGuestFieldJump (OwnJumpRule: the host's position lane reads 0 while
+    //        it loads 350, so dest == LastHostField would bounce it into a 352 reload) and the follow holds while my control is off
+    //        (HubHoldMs, counted from the title card's close: CaptionRestamps). DEST phase on the own jump's landing (LandingStep: the
+    //        landing decides, so a same-field ATE counts): the follow holds while my control is off (TailHoldMs from its first held tick:
+    //        Finding 4's capped hold, scoped here), and the copy's own scripted Field() out goes where the host is (DestJump: the host's
+    //        announced field, else the field it stands on, else the hub) -- never a bounce into a reload of the ATE field. Every own jump
+    //        that is not rewritten keeps my copy's own entrance through the landing's mirror (OwnEntranceRule). An own exit that beat the
+    //        host out of the ATE field -- the host still there with the entrance my copy's ATE ran on -- holds the follow back into it
